  "first_generation_response": {
    "turn_id": "turn_000003",
    "event_index": 3,
    "role": "assistant",
    "text": "Certainly! The following regular expression can be used to match the ULID (Universally Unique Lexicographically Sortable Identifier) format:\n\n```regex\n^[0-9A-HJKMNP-TV-Z]{26}$\n```\n\nExplanation:\n- `^` asserts the start of the string.\n- `[0-9A-HJKMNP-TV-Z]` matches any character in the range 0-9, A-H, J-K, M-N, P-T, or V-Z.\n- `{26}` specifies that the preceding character class should occur exactly 26 times (the length of a ULID).\n- `$` asserts the end of the string.\n\nNote that ULIDs are case-sensitive and use a modified base32 encoding, excluding the characters I, L, O, and Q to avoid confusion with numerals."
  },
